Analysis & Design document

1.Analyse and check the feasibility of including all the below fields in the check-in email
- Operating airline and flight number
- Marketing airline and flight number
- Record locator for operating airline
- Record locator for ticketing airline
- Customer baggage allowance
- Contact information for questions
- Customer seat information
- Check-in details (terminal, airline, channel)
- Information where to check flight status
- Terminal information/Flight information for connecting flights
- How to provide feedback after travel
2.Analyze to retrieve the email address from CTCE SSR instead of the passenger EmailAddress attribute, if it is not available at the reservation level                                                                                                                      
3.Analyse to display the operating airline, operating flight number, marketing airline, marketing airline flight number, record locator for ticketing airline in the check-in email only when the Operating Airline Code and Marketing Airline Code are different in the TripSearch API response
4.Analyse to display the seat information if avaialble from the sabre response along with the passenger's name in the check-in email
5.Analyse to include all connecting flight information belonging to the same trip group to display in the check-in email. This will include: Departure Airport, Arrival Airport, Flight Number, Departure Date & Time and Check-in Terminal    
6.Analysing all the new fields with sample CERT and PROD PNRs 
7.Analyse all the new fields to include in the email template                                                                                                                                 
8.Prepare Solution design document.


Develoment, Unit Testing

1. To retrieve the email address from CTCE SSR instead of the passenger EmailAddress attribute, if it is not available at the reservation level  
2. To display the operating airline, operating flight number, marketing airline, marketing airline flight number, record locator for ticketing airline in the check-in email only when the Operating Airline Code and Marketing Airline Code are different in the TripSearch API response.               
3. To include the customer's baggage allowance in the check-in email that is obtained from the GetPassengerData API response      
4. To display the seat information if avaialble from the sabre response along with the passenger's name in the check-in email
5. To display the check-in terminal in the check-in email if the terminal information is available for a flight. To display check-in airline and chennel details in the check-in email with fixed data.
6. To include all connecting flight information belonging to the same trip group to display in the check-in email. This will include: Departure Airport, Arrival Airport, Flight Number, Departure Date & Time and Check-in Terminal (Terminal information of each connecting flight will be obtained by calling getFlightInfo API
7. To update both the CDG station email template and normal email template to include all the new fields
8. Unit Testing and Test case document preparation


